Advanced seminar: a sustained textual and argumentative study (@greek-seminar-study: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @greek-scholarly-path, #philosophy @greek-independent-research, #ancient-greek-philosophy @greek-independent-research) { r_7WN2AF9HW3X3BNQSTF5CKFJ22Q
Choose a problem from the [seminar families](seminars/Seminars.lingua#r_5FTSQDJTR924S9Z0G9EDBQFR1Y). Define the question, primary corpus, language preparation, critical edition, and scholarly debate before writing. A chapter comparison should belong to a reading of the complete relevant dialogue, treatise, or connected books, with its argument sequence understood.

Use [a Greek textual dossier](Philological-study.lingua#r_353E4E4WH3BWFHHJNZMPKBPEXF) and [the literature dossier](Scholarly-inquiry.lingua#r_2FEBDJ8R5JDHXX54TSATY2CRVZ). The same dossiers can support several investigations.

**Required product:** a sustained seminar study with a defensible thesis, close analyses, reconstruction of competing interpretations, objections, replies, and a bibliography distinguishing primary texts, editions, translations, and scholarship. Explain how the selected passages fit the whole work and why the issue matters.

Present the work for discussion. A reader should be able to question the interpretation, its Greek, its account of the literature, and the inference from evidence to conclusion. Produce a revised study and explain what the criticism changed.

Length follows the problem's actual demands. A short note that only repeats a doctrine, a list of quotations, or a bibliography without an argument does not meet this outcome.

For the full study, complete two seminar studies addressing different problem families. At least one must develop a substantive comparison across texts, authors, traditions, or a well-defined disciplinary crossing. Reusing research is appropriate when the second study contributes a distinct investigation rather than merely relabelling the same work.

**Continue:** [Independent research](Independent-research.lingua#r_08YBJ1G76KSJ3QTG42FKCCAV5K). **Return:** [Research progression](Research.lingua#r_434NMA510XG7R81DAAG64PZX09).
